Template: rustyrig-server/admin-password
Type: password
Default:
Description: Password for the RustyRig admin account:
 Choose the password used to log in as the RustyRig admin user.  This is
 required when creating a new server database.  An existing database is not
 changed during upgrades.

Template: rustyrig-server/enable-guest
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Enable the shared guest account?
 Guests log in with username "guest" and password "guest". The shipped guest
 permissions allow receive audio and chat only. Enable this if you want
 shared guest access to your LAN/VPN station.
 .
 The account is disabled by default. This choice applies only when creating
 a new server database; existing accounts are preserved during upgrades.

Template: rustyrig/admin-users
Type: string
Default:
Description: Local users to add to the rradmin group:
 Enter existing local usernames separated by spaces. Members can read,
 modify and delete RustyRig logs and maintain its SQLite databases.
 Leave empty to add nobody. Existing group members are retained.
 Users must log in again after being added to the group.

Template: rustyrig/serial-users
Type: string
Default:
Description: Local users to add to the rruser device-access group:
 Enter existing local usernames separated by spaces. Members can open
 RustyRig virtual serial ports (including CAT and GPS) created by rrclient.
 This is separate from rradmin and does not grant administrative permissions.
 Leave empty to add nobody. Existing memberships are preserved.
 Members must log out and back in for new group access.

Template: rustyrig-server/backlight-video-group
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Allow the RustyRig server to control local display backlights?
 Add the rustyrig service account to the system video group, allowing
 access to backlight devices such as /sys/class/backlight/*/brightness
 where that group grants write permission.
 .
 This may also grant access to other video devices. Choose No if the
 server does not need local display control.

Template: rustyrig-server/serial-dialout-group
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Allow the RustyRig server to access local serial devices?
 Add the rustyrig service account to the system dialout group, commonly
 used for USB serial interfaces and radio CAT control ports.
 .
 This grants access to other serial devices in the group as well.
 Choose No if the server does not require local serial hardware.
